cret wars without  having the mutants there and without  having the fantastic four however the  fantastic four are going to be released  late 2024 and the last avengers film  avengers secret wars comes out late 2025  that means the fantastic four will have  only been in the mcu for a year and if  they put the x-men somewhere in phase 6  the x-men won't have even been in the  mcu for a year before we get to secret  wars but here's why this is actually a  good thing there are 5 major reasons why  phase 7 is going to completely blow away  any other phase that we've got so far in  the mcu and this starts with the end of  phase six it's a good thing that the  x-men and the fantastic four are only  going to be introduced at the end of  phase six because that means it's just  going to be a little tease of who they  actually are we'll have one movie about  the fantastic four and maybe the mutants  will appear in a couple of projects then  they will team up and they will fight in  secret wars however like i said this is  just a tease a glimpse of what the  fantastic four can do and who the  mutants are actually going to be because  i don't believe they will introduce a  lot of mutants before secret wars there  are a lot of spots in phase 6 but we  already know a lot of the films or  projects that are going to be coming out  like armor wars or deadpool or nova  projects that have already been  announced but don't have official  release dates are most likely going to  fill these slots of phase 6 which means  we'll probably only get one or two  projects with the mutants in them so  phase 6 and the multiverse saga ends  with a slight introduction to the  fantastic four and the mutants and then  in phase seven is where we pick up and  we get really introduced to them so  reasons one and two of the five points  of why phase seven is going to blow us  away are the x-men and the fantastic  four of course but really diving into  who they actually are really diving into  bigger stories and most importantly the  connectivity that the mcu offers we will  have individual mutant projects and  x-men projects that will focus on  specific characters but also  interconnect with other x-men projects  with other fantastic four projects and  of course still avengers projects and of  course the same goes for the fantastic  four they will interact with other x-men  and they will interact with other  avengers however reed richards is going  to be a very important and pivotal  character of phase seven why well  because he is the smartest man alive and  he is going to be a crucial component in  beating the next big bad of the next  saga which is going to be galactus which  is actually 0.4 and not 0.3 0.3 is one  of galactus's heralds which i'm assuming  is going to be the silver server now of  course we've gotten a silver surfer  movie before the fantastic four the rise  of the silver surfer so there is always  the thought that marvel studios might  want to stay away from the silver surfer  for a while and introduce another  fantastic four villain however we are  expecting dr doom to appear in the mcu  quite soon and we know that he'll  probably play a major role in secret  wars and could even be the main villain  on top of king giving us god emperor  doom but having said that i do not  believe that he's going to be done in  phase six i think he's going to continue  on in the mcu at least i hope but point  three of why phase seven is going to be  awesome is cause we are going to be  introduced to a herald of galactus and i  hope it's the silver surfer now here's  where reed richards and the fantastic  four come in they're going to come in  contact with the silver surfer but i  think most of us know how that story  goes ultimately the silver surfer is  typically convinced that earth is worth  saving and defies galactus he then works  alongside the fantastic four and other  heroes who will be in the mcu at that  point in time to defeat galactus but  this is going to be a huge event  galactus is going to be the kang or the  doom of phase 7 and phase 8 and maybe  even phase 9. depending on how long they  want to take it but galactus will be the  big bad of the next saga which could be  the galactus saga i've seen a lot of fan  art out there that says the age of  galactus and i really like that title  now galactus has been defeated many  different times in the comics and  sometimes it's not even that hard  literally squirrel girl defeated him  well not really defeated him but kept  him from consuming the earth by simply  being his friend and giving him some  nuts no i don't think that's going to  happen in the mcu of course i think it's  ultimately going to come down to the  ultimate nullifier most comic book fans  know what this is it's the ultimate  weapon that can defeat galactus and it's  actually kept on galactus ship however  in the mcu i think reed richards in the  fantastic four and maybe even some other  smart people like bruce banner if he's  still around will be the ones to create  the ultimate nullifier however i also  believe that there is one more point  that is going to make phase seven and  beyond pretty epic and that is the  cosmic entities now galactus himself is  a cosmic entity he's a cosmic being and  marvel studios recently has kind of been  preparing us for cosmic beans they  mentioned the living tribunal in doctor  strange we actually saw the living  tribunal and doctor strange in the  multiverse of madness and they  introduced eternity in thor love and  thunder however eternity was very  different than his comic counterpart but  even though the cosmic entities might be  a little bit different i do believe  they'll have some major roles to play in  phase 7 and beyond which i hope  ultimately leads up to some avengers  x-men and fantastic four kind of teaming  up with some cosmic entities we know the  watcher exists in the mcu we saw the  statue of the watcher in thor love and  thunder and in guardians o